#basePath P3_Sterile
#include "Header.leaf"

:: Start
@exposed
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// "NONE" ensures no other threads are in-progress
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "NONE", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "FieldStationSterile"
@cutscene
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()

// Mark start of thread
$set global:currentThread = "P3_Sterile"
$call DecreaseTime(1)

// Adds flavor text if player has finished talking to aquaculture specialist
$if !HasSeen(P3_CiscoPop.End)
{@}   
       Neveah's portrait stares at you from it's place on the dash. 
$elseif !HasSeen(P3_TroutPop.End) // I'm not sure what the or function is, which is why the code looks like this
{@}   
       Neveah's portrait stares at you from it's place on the dash. 
$endif

{@}
       Adding fish to the lake is possible, and if you remember correctly, there was another way of changing populations beyond that...
       Just as the thought crosses your mind, a sign for a Biological Field Station passes by. 

{@You}
       What beautiful timing. 

{@}
       You stop at a small building by the edge of a tributary and get out of your car.
       Just as you are about to knock on the door, it swings open. 

{@Robertson}
       Hello, ma'am.

{@You}
       Holy s-
       You scared me. 

{@Robertson}
       My apologies, ma'am. 
       I simply like to be... proactive.

{@}
       You can tell they are containing a laugh. 

{@Robertson}
       What brings you to my neck of the woods?

{@}
       Sterilization. You mentioned that you used to do it. 

{@Robertson}
       Yes, ma'am. That we did. 
       We still have a small program up and running, if you'd like to see.

{@You}
       That would be really nice. 

{@Robertson}
       Of course, ma'am. Here, follow me.

{@}
       Robertson leads you to a tank filled with squirming sea lamprey. 

{@Robertson}
       We catch male sea lamprey from traps in the tributaries. 
       Then, we inject 'em with a chemosterilant.
       That's a fancy word for a chemical that makes the sea lamprey unable to reproduce. 
       We tag 'em, for science purposes, and then release 'em in tributaries where sea lampreys mate.

{@}
       Robertson reaches into the tank and pulls out a single sea lamprey.

{@Robertson}
       The female sea lamprey can't tell 'em apart from non-sterilized sea lamprey. 
       Wouldn't work if we gave 'em the ick, you know. 

{@}
       They give you a wink. The sea lamprey continues to worm around their palms.

{@Robertson}
       Wanna hold it?

{@You}
       Not particularly. 

{@Robertson}
       It'll be fine. Here ya go...

{@}
       There's a sea lamprey in your hands, looking up at you. 
       It's smaller than you thought it would be, given its reputation. 

{@You}
       He's... kinda cute.

{@Robertson}
       Yes, ma'am, they grow on ya. 
       Ok, back into the tank, little guy. 

{@}
       You release the sea lamprey back with his brethren. 
       He's gone in a undulating tide of smooth scales as soon as you let go. 

{@Robertson}
       There're only a few right now, and these'll get released soon at the lampricide tributary site.
       But if you'd like to expand the program, that can always be done. 
       //evidence chip
$call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-sterilization")

{@You}
       Thanks, Robertson. 
       And thanks for letting me hold one. 

{@Robertson}
       What can I say? It's my favorite part of the job. 

{@}
       The two of you laugh together.
// TODO: Rest of thread here

// TODO: Give evidence chip

$call UnlockLocation(FieldStationLampricide)
$call EnableMapButton()


:: AtFieldStationLampricide
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "P3_Sterile", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "FieldStationLampricide"
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()

{@}   
       Claire is waiting for you at the edge of the river, tanks filled with sea lamprey by the building.

{@Claire}
       Young scientist! What a pleasure it is to see you!

{@You}
       It's good to see you, too, Claire. You seem ready to go.

{@Claire}
       I am always ready to go! And in this particular moment that statement is very true!
       The sterilized sea lamprey are ready to be released, thanks to my beloved Robertson.

{@You}
       Your... beloved Robertson?

{@Claire}
       Why, yes! We are to be wed this fall!

{@You}
       That's pretty perfect. Congrats.

{@Claire}
       Thank you! Now, it is time for release!

{@}
       Together with Claire, you spend a few hours transferring the sea lamprey from the tank into the river.
       Finally, the tanks are empty, and you collapse to the ground, spent.
$call GiveActionCard("Action-release-sterilized")

{@You}
       Well, that's done.

{@Claire}
       Be free, Sir Sea Lampreys! Have fun!

{@}
       You chuckle. Claire sits next to you.

{@Claire}
       Come to my wedding, young scientist. 

{@You}
       Really?
       I mean, I'm honored, but you just met me?

{@Claire}
       Yes. It will be fun. And your uncles will be there.

{@You}
       Ah, so you know my uncles.

{@Claire}
       Everyone knows your uncles, young scientist.
       ...
       It's good to have you back, Ana. It's always good to see people come home. 

{@}
       You look out onto the calm river, and you can almost see a younger version of you spending summers in the water.

{@You}
       Yeah. You're right.

// TODO: Rest of Field Station (Lampricide) section here

// TODO: Give action card


// skip to end
$goto .End


:: End
@exposed
@tracked

// Mark end of thread
$set global:currentThread = "NONE"

// Go to Phase 2 Continue Hub
$goto P3_Hub.Continue